Add QtTesting + PythonQt include directories for system (non-superbuild) builds.

In Slicer's own superbuild the QtTesting and PythonQt build trees are injected
onto the include path implicitly. A system build has no such wiring: CTK's
CTK_INCLUDE_DIRS does not carry either header dir, and the installed CTK headers
in /usr/include/ctk-0.1/ reference these third-party headers directly:
  - ctkQtTestingUtility.h -> <pqTestUtility.h>, <pqWidgetEventPlayer.h>
  - ctkAbstractPythonManager.h -> <PythonQtPythonInclude.h>
Many Slicer targets include those CTK headers transitively while linking only
CTKWidgets (not CTKQtTesting / a PythonQt-bearing CTK lib), so they never
inherit the third-party include dirs. Add both globally at the top level (each
gated on the matching Slicer_USE_* option); also keep the targeted
Libs/MRML/Widgets wiring for its AUTOMOC step.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-03 14:52:02.134187416 -0700
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-03 14:52:02.146163652 -0700
@@ -1010,6 +1010,17 @@
 find_package(CTK REQUIRED)
 include(${CTK_USE_FILE})

+# System (non-superbuild) QtTesting: CTK's CTK_INCLUDE_DIRS does not carry the
+# QtTesting header dir, yet several Slicer targets (qSlicerBaseQTGUI's
+# qSlicerApplication.cxx, Base/QTApp, Base/QTCLI) #include the installed
+# ctkQtTestingUtility.h directly, which pulls in <pqTestUtility.h>. Those
+# targets link CTKWidgets, not CTKQtTesting, so they never inherit qttesting's
+# include dir. Add it globally so every subdirectory can compile.
+if(Slicer_USE_QtTesting)
+  find_package(QtTesting REQUIRED)
+  include_directories(${QtTesting_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+endif()
+
 #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Update CMake module path
 #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -1068,6 +1079,12 @@
   # See https://github.com/commontk/PythonQt/issues/7
   # and https://github.com/commontk/PythonQt/issues/8
   find_package(PythonQt REQUIRED)
+  # System (non-superbuild) PythonQt: installed CTK headers such as
+  # ctkAbstractPythonManager.h #include <PythonQtPythonInclude.h> and other
+  # PythonQt headers directly. CTK_INCLUDE_DIRS does not carry PythonQt's
+  # include dir, so add it globally here (covers every subdirectory, e.g.
+  # Modules/Loadable/SubjectHierarchy).
+  include_directories(${PYTHONQT_INCLUDE_DIRS})
   link_directories(${PYTHONQT_INSTALL_DIR}/lib)
   include(ctkMacroWrapPythonQt)
   include(ctkMacroCompilePythonScript)
--- a/Libs/MRML/Widgets/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-02 15:46:36.204091766 -0700
+++ b/Libs/MRML/Widgets/CMakeLists.txt	2026-06-02 15:46:36.216875345 -0700
@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@
   list(APPEND CTK_LIBRARIES
     CTKQtTesting
     )
+  # In a non-superbuild (system QtTesting) build, CTKQtTesting does not
+  # re-export the QtTesting include directory, yet Slicer's qMRML*EventPlayer
+  # and qMRML*EventTranslator headers include <pqWidgetEventPlayer.h> and
+  # other pq* headers directly. Resolve the QtTesting imported target and add
+  # its include dirs so the sources and AUTOMOC-generated moc files compile.
+  find_package(QtTesting REQUIRED)
+  include_directories(${QtTesting_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 endif()

 # --------------------------------------------------------------------------
